r"""patch_L494_3_arrows_and_triad_20261026.py -- direction arrows on the orbits and paths,
and the whole triad opens the frame note. Tony's phone look of Oct 26,
night.

Built on gallery 1e6f6691a756cafcd5df721b2251b74769110c77 at
https://github.com/tonylquintanilla/tonyquintanilla.github.io (branch
main), with orrery 8f4173c4cb28abfdac622b54ed33031e169f6c66 at
https://github.com/tonylquintanilla/palomas_orrery.

WHAT IT DOES, all or nothing

    1. A small flat arrowhead on each body's orbit or path in the Solar
       System room, 5 arrow lengths ahead of the body, pointing the way it
       travels. The direction is read from the served points, which run
       the way the body moves, so Halley and Ikeya-Seki point clockwise
       and the planets counterclockwise. The arrow keeps its size on the
       screen through a zoom, and is not drawn when its place is outside
       the view or the orbit is too small for it at that scale. Tony chose
       the flat arrowhead ("B") and the distance ("B") from renders.
    2. The whole x, y, z triad opens the frame note, not only the Aries
       glyph.

WHAT IT EDITS

    gallery/direction_arrows.js (new): where each arrow goes.
    documentation/smoke_direction_arrows.js (new): its check, six worked
        cases and the page's wiring, with a self-test that breaks the
        file three ways first.
    interactive.html: the arrows in the Solar System room, the triad,
        the change note.
    gallery_maintenance_run.py: runs the new check (it gates), and the
        live check fetches the new file.
    tools/headless/walk_solar_system_drawer.js: Claude's room walk.

    No data changes, so no build is needed: it reaches a visitor on the
    push.

HOW TO RUN

    Save it in the website folder (tonyquintanilla.github.io), open it
    in VS Code and press Run. It prints an "ok" line per file and "patch
    applied"; a second run refuses. Then gallery_maintenance_run.py,
    which should be green, with "Direction arrows" among the checks; move
    this file into documentation\, commit and push. Undo before a commit
    is Discard Changes in GitHub Desktop; the two new files are then
    deleted in File Explorer.

Written October 26, 2026 with Anthropic's Claude Opus 5.5.
"""
